infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title mypy vs pyright: same core, useful divergence
  desc Either beats none — pick by speed, inference, and ORM plugins
  compares
    - label mypy
      children
        - label Python reference implementation
          desc The spec's own checker; the dmypy daemon makes warm re-checks fast
        - label Slower on large codebases
          desc Full runs take minutes where pyright takes seconds
        - label Skips unannotated defs by default
          desc Treats unannotated functions as Any and never reads their bodies
        - label Django + SQLAlchemy plugins
          desc Understands ORM magic — often the deciding factor in those stacks
    - label pyright
      children
        - label TypeScript, the Pylance engine
          desc Microsoft's checker inside VS Code, with a watch mode
        - label Substantially faster on big repos
          desc Minute-long mypy runs finish in seconds to tens of seconds
        - label Infers and checks unannotated code
          desc Catches int + str behind an inferred return mypy never reads
        - label Stronger inference
          desc Adoption surfaces a wave of pre-existing errors on day one
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
